\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li270\sl202\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0   Now I have found the ground wherein
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 Sure my soul's anchor may remain
\par The wounds of Jesus, for my sin
\par Before the world's foundation slain;
\par Whose mercy shall unshaken stay,
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj\i ://:When heaven and earth are fled  away. ://:
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Father, Thine everlasting  grace
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 Our scanty thought surpasses far,
\par Thy heart still melts with tenderness,
\par \pard\li270\sl202\slmult0  Thy arms of love still open are
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 Returning sinners to receive,
\par \i  ://:That mercy they may taste and live. ://:
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. O love, Thou bottomless abyss,
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj My sins are swallowed up in Thee!
\par Covered is my unrighteousness,
\par Nor spot of guilt remains on me,
\par While Jesu's blood through earth and skies
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\i  ://:Mercy, free, boundless mercy! Cries. ://:
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With faith I plunge me in this sea,
\par \pard\li180\sl200\slmult0  Here is my hope, my joy, my rest;
\par  Hither, when hell assails, I flee,
\par  I look into my Saviour's breast:
\par \pard\li144\sl200\slmult0  Away, sad doubt and anxious fear!
\par \pard\sl200\slmult0\qj\i    ://:Mercy is all that's written there.://\i0 :
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Though waves and storms go o'er  my head,
\par \pard\li144\sl200\slmult0\qj  Though strength, and health, 
\par and friends be gone,
\par \pard\li144\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\fs16\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0\fs24 
\par \pard\li144\sl200\slmult0\qj  Though joys be withered all and dead,
\par  Though every comfort be withdrawn,
\par  On this my steadfast soul relies
\par \i  ://:Father, Thy mercy never dies! ://:
\par \i0 
\par \pard\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Fixed on this ground will I remain,
\par \pard\li144\sl200\slmult0\qj  Though my heart fail and flesh decay;
\par  This anchor shall my soul sustain,
\par  When earth's foundations melt away:
\par  Mercy's full power I then shall prove,
\par \pard\i   ://:Loved with an everlasting love. ://:\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

